(a) Term defined. The term "problem dog" means any dog that has or exhibits any one or more of the following characteristics:
(1) Any dog that is a stray with no known owner;
(2) Any dog that harms any person or damages any person's property other than that of its owner;
(3) Any dog that shows aggression outside its owner's premises when not under the control of its owner;
(4) Any dog that runs in packs of more than two;
(5) Any dog that is abandoned; and
(6) Any dog that is severely injured or sick and not in its owner's care.
(b) City's remedies. Any problem dog may be subdued and taken to a veterinary hospital for appropriate humane disposition. The reasonable costs of boarding and disposition shall be paid by the city.
(c) Administrator. The initial administrator and enforcement officer under this division shall be the county marshal who shall consult with the Mayor as substantial issues arise.
(d) Initial enforcement. Unless otherwise directed by the Mayor, initial enforcement of this division shall only occur after receipt of one or more citizen complaints.
(Ord. No. 91410-101, §§ 1—4, 9-14-2010)

